WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
you were here in 2015

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.570 line:92%
right after you announced,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when you announced
that time,

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was not as big of a deal
as it was this time.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:11.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were -- "New York Times"
put it on A21.

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A19.
-A19. Oh, yeah.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But who's counting?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot has changed.
One thing that's changed

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the party has moved
more to the left,

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also you --
it is a more crowded field.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems like a lot of people
are jumping in here.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:28.128
Do you, having gone through what
you went through four years ago,

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
feel more prepared?
-I do.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think
what I'm excited about

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that many of the ideas
that we talked about

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.236 size:88% position:44% line:92%
three or four years ago,

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:39.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
which at that time were
thought to be crazy

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
and extreme and radical,
are now supported

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
by a considerable majority
of the American people.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, four years ago,
when we talked about

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
raising the minimum wage
to a living wage,

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:52.118
15 bucks an hour --
"Oh, my God. You can't do that."

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.954
Five states have already
done it in the last year.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:58.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's progress.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.694 line:92%
You know, we talked about

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:05.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
ending the disgrace
of the United States being

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.433 line:92%
the only major country on Earth

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
not to guarantee healthcare
to all people

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
through a Medicare for All
single payer program.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.640 line:92%
Crazy idea four years ago,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.142
majority of the American people
support it today,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.578 size:84% position:42%
and that's important.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:23.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because healthcare --
Seth, to my mind,

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.151 line:92%
healthcare is a human right,

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it should not matter
whether you're rich,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.254 size:75% position:38% line:92%
whether you're poor,

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make certain
that your kid gets

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
the best possible
healthcare available.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.259 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That's what we gotta do.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.162
Public colleges
and universities, tuition free.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's now an idea
that is spreading

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.132 size:81% position:41% line:92%
all over this country.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:42.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
And importantly,
four years ago, I said

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:47.507
we have got to stand up to
the fossil fuel industry.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:50.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have got to transform
our energy system

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.313 size:78% position:39%
away from fossil fuel
to energy efficiency

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.715 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and sustainable energy.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think more and more
people understand

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
that climate change
is an existential threat

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.989
to this planet, and we have got
to be aggressive

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
in transforming
our energy system.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.060 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.194 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I want to ask this.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of those issues
obviously distinguished you

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.832 line:92%
from the competition last time.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.268 size:84% position:42%
One of the successes is
you now have convinced

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.270
a lot of the people that
are running against you...

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Do you ever want to say --

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause a lot of them obviously
are friends or colleagues.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:22.008
Do you ever want to say,
"Hey, this is kind of my --

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
Medicare for All,
that's kind of mine"?

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.377 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or are you happy that it is
now an consensus?

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am. Look.
Nobody, you know --

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
nobody -- no one person
can do it alone.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we need a lot of voices
out there.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.188
One of the things also --
you asked me the difference

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.489 size:78% position:39% line:92%
between now and then.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the first week
of our campaign, Seth,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have signed up
1 million volunteers

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are prepared
to roll up their sleeves

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:48.401
and get to work not only to
help me win the nomination

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to defeat
the most dangerous president

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.506 line:92%
in modern history, Mr. Trump...

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
...but also to help us
take on

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
the very powerful
special interests --

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wall Street,
the fossil fuel industry,

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:07.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the military
industrial complex --

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.555 line:92%
that have just so much power

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:10.957
over the economic and political
life of this country.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.693
-So many senators running.
Obviously, you see them.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.827 line:92%
They are your colleagues.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it awkward
that you all know

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're all trying
to be president?

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.102 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know, look...

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.672 line:92%
-I'll take that as a yes.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.608
-The short answer is yes.
-Yeah, okay, I got it.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.376
That's human. I would say
that's a human reaction.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.079 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, we all have lunch
together every Tuesday,

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.249
and you got half the caucus
running for -- for president.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.151
You know what I'm saying?
It is kind of strange,

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:41.721
but on the other hand, you know,
we have known each other --

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've known Elizabeth Warren
for like 20 years.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:48.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've known many of the other
senators for a long time,

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.062 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and we're friends.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think what all of us
understand --

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:54.500
obviously each and every one of
us wants to win the nomination.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.802 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I certainly do.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:59.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think we all understand
that no matter who wins,

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:03.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody is going to rally
around that candidate

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.310 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and defeat Donald Trump.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.412 size:84% position:42%
That is most important.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.114 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-That's nice to hear.

